[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792777807-2042744051.jpg[/img][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b]What it does[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Every marker on the world map[/b]: spires, altars, sanctums, vaults, lairs, towns, camps, mines, caves, garrisons, quests, lore rumors, graves, and all 448 gold and 1032 silver chests.
[*][b]A Map Key & Filters panel[/b] built from the game's own UI art: an icon, a count and an ON/OFF switch for every marker type, whole categories at a click, completed quests and filters for your custom pins.
[*][b]Find on the map[/b]: press [b]Shift+F[/b], type a name or a kind of place, and the map moves to show it.
[*][b]Fog and pin modes[/b]: the game's own fog, a light fog over a fully drawn map, or no fog; and pins only where you've been, grayed out in unexplored land, or all of them.
[*][b]Looted chests[/b]: open a chest and it's hidden or grayed out with a check mark, until it comes back.

[*][b]A minimap on your HUD[/b] with the map's terrain, the time of day or the weather, and other players, that you can move, resize and zoom.
[*][b]All 15 game languages[/b]: the mod's text follows the game's language.
[*][b]Client only[/b]: works in single player, hosted games and on any dedicated server. Nothing goes on the server, and other players don't need it.
[/list]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792776524-663559092.jpg[/img][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b]The Map Key & Filters panel[/b][/size]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792776524-727906371.jpg[/img][/center]

[list]
[*][b]Every gold and silver chest in the world is included[/b]: all 448 gold chests and 1032 silver chests have their own rows in the filter, so you can show just the chests you're hunting.
[*]Click a row to show or hide that marker type.
[*]Click a category header to switch the whole category; [b]+ / -[/b] folds it.
[*][b]COMPLETED QUESTS[/b] (off at first) shows the quests you've finished; Main Quest and Side Quest show the ones you're on.
[*][b]CUSTOM PINS[/b]: click a pin icon to show or hide your own pins of that kind.
[*][b]Tab[/b] (or the - button at the top) folds the panel away. The [b]cog[/b] opens Settings.
[/list]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792777143-1153363650.jpg[/img][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b]Find (Shift+F)[/b][/size]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792776528-804463773.jpg[/img][/center]

On the world map, press [b]Shift+F[/b] or click [b]FIND[/b]. Type a name or a kind of place, for example [i]gold[/i], [i]spire[/i] or [i]garrison[/i]. Every match is listed with its region, its distance from you, and [i][Locked][/i] if you haven't unlocked it yet.
[list]
[*]Click a result twice, double-click it or press [b]Enter[/b], and the map moves to show it.
[*][b]All Matching Places - Zoom to fit[/b] shows every match at once.
[*][b]F2[/b] (or [b]Ctrl+F[/b]) switches whether Find skips marker types you've hidden with the filters.
[*][b]Esc[/b] or [b]Shift+F[/b] closes it.
[/list]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792777201-1180845193.jpg[/img][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b]Settings[/b][/size]

[center][img]UPLOAD:05-settings.jpg[/img][/center]

The [b]cog[/b] on the Map Key (and the one under the minimap) opens Settings:
[list]
[*][b]SHOW ALL / HIDE ALL[/b] switch every marker type at once.
[*][b]FOG:[/b] [b]EXPLORED[/b] is the game's own fog, [b]HYBRID[/b] draws the whole map with unexplored land under a light fog, [b]REVEAL ALL[/b] has no fog.
[*][b]PINS:[/b] [b]EXPLORED[/b] shows pins only where you've been, [b]HYBRID[/b] grays out pins in unexplored land, [b]REVEAL ALL[/b] shows every pin.
[*][b]Custom Marker Size[/b]: the size of your own pins.
[*][b]Show Minimap[/b], [b]Minimap Terrain[/b] and [b]Minimap Icon[/b] (sun/moon or weather).
[*][b]Looted Chests[/b]: hide them or gray them out.
[/list]
Everything is remembered.

[line]

[size=4][b]Looted chests[/b][/size]

[center][img]UPLOAD:11-looted-chests.jpg[/img][/center]

Open a gold or silver chest and the mod marks it looted: hidden, or grayed out with a check mark. On the world map, [b]Ctrl + left click[/b] a chest to mark it or clear the mark. A looted chest comes back after 30 minutes of play unless it's in a Flame Altar's build zone. Looted chests are saved per world.

If you open chests with another key than E, set [i]InteractKey=[/i] under [i][Chests][/i] in [i]minimap_config.ini[/i]; [i]RespawnMinutes=[/i] is there too.

[line]

[size=4][b]Minimap[/b][/size]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792776532-1239715886.jpg[/img][/center]

A minimap on your HUD with the World Map's terrain, a compass, the time of day (or the weather) and its zoom level, placed under the Journal [J] tab at first. Cleared places and looted chests show a check mark.

[b]Hold Shift + Alt[/b] to set it up. The mouse cursor appears and the camera stops turning, so you won't swing your view or attack. While you hold them:
[list]
[*][b]Drag the minimap[/b] to move it anywhere on screen.
[*][b]Drag its bottom-right corner[/b] to make it bigger or smaller.
[*][b]Mouse wheel[/b] zooms.
[*][b]Double-click the star at the top[/b] to put it back in its default place.
[/list]
Zoom any time with [b][[/b] and [b]][/b] (or numpad - and +), or with the - / + buttons under the minimap; the [b]cog[/b] next to them opens Settings. [b]Other Players[/b] in the panel shows other players on the map, and on the minimap as colored arrows that point where they're heading. Position, size and zoom are saved for next time.

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792776534-363048547.jpg[/img][/center]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792777343-1199341688.jpg[/img][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Close Enshrouded.
[*]Open the game folder (Steam: right-click Enshrouded > Manage > Browse local files).
[*]Copy everything from the zip into it, keeping the folders: [b]dbgcore.dll[/b] next to [i]enshrouded.exe[/i], and the [b]greeneye\unlock-map-markers[/b] folder.
[*]Start the game and open the map (M).
[/list]

[b]Servers:[/b] nothing to install. The mod only runs on your own game.

[b]Install by hand:[/b] Vortex does not know the Greeneye Loader yet.

[b]Uninstall:[/b] delete [i]greeneye\unlock-map-markers[/i]. If no other Greeneye mod is left, also delete [i]dbgcore.dll[/i] and the [i]greeneye[/i] folder.

[line]

[size=4][b]Languages[/b][/size]

The mod's text follows the game's language: English, German, French, Italian, Spanish, Portuguese (Brazil), Polish, Russian, Ukrainian, Turkish, Japanese, Korean, Simplified Chinese, Traditional Chinese and Thai. Marker and region names come from the game itself.

To use another language, set [i]Language=[/i] in [i]greeneye\unlock-map-markers\minimap_config.ini[/i] under [i][General][/i]: [i]auto[/i] (follows the game), or [i]english, german, french, italian, spanish, brazilian, polish, russian, ukrainian, turkish, japanese, koreana, schinese, tchinese, thai[/i]. Restart the game after changing it.

The translations are my own. If something reads wrong in your language, please say so in the Posts tab.

[line]

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Single player, hosting your own game, and dedicated servers[/b], all with the mod on your game only.
[*][b]Plays well with other mods.[/b] It runs through the Greeneye Loader ([i]dbgcore.dll[/i], shared with Find, Quick Deposit, Continue and Embervale Teleport). Where another mod hooks the same game function, it chains onto that hook instead of replacing it.
[*]With the [b]Find[/b] mod installed, Find on the map uses Find's search box.
[*][b]Safe on game updates.[/b] Made for the current game version. If an update changes code the mod patches, it skips that part instead of crashing, and the log says so.
[*]Works with Steam. Not tested with other store versions.
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]Troubleshooting[/b][/size]

If something doesn't work, please post these files with your report. Both are in the game folder:
[list]
[*][i]greeneye\unlock-map-markers\unlock_map_markers.log[/i]: what the mod found and patched.
[*][i]greeneye\loader.log[/i]: what the Greeneye Loader did.
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]Changelog[/b][/size]

[b]1.2.0[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Settings[/b] (the cog on the Map Key, and under the minimap): Show All / Hide All, fog, the new pin modes, custom marker size, minimap on or off, minimap terrain, sun/moon or weather, and looted chests hidden or grayed out.
[*][b]Pin modes[/b]: EXPLORED shows pins only where you've been, HYBRID grays out pins in unexplored land, REVEAL ALL shows them all. Requested by dremen and KazarusKain.
[*][b]Completed quests[/b] have their own filter (off at first), so Main Quest and Side Quest show only the quests you're on. Requested by inShaneity, KazarusKain and Deadcow67.
[*][b]Looted chests[/b]: open a gold or silver chest and it's marked looted, hidden or grayed out with a check mark. Ctrl + left click a chest on the map to mark it or clear the mark. Chests come back after 30 minutes of play unless they're in a Flame Altar's build zone. Saved per world. Requested by inShaneity and FWSWBN.
[*][b]Minimap[/b]: the World Map's terrain under it and check marks on cleared places (requested by inShaneity), weather in place of the sun or moon (requested by Loling91), an option to hide it (requested by FWSWBN), and other players as colored arrows that show where they're heading.
[*][b]Custom Marker Size[/b] for your own pins. Requested by dremen.
[*]The map's hint bar shows the mod's keys: Ctrl+click, Shift+F and Tab.
[*]Reported bugs fixed: none.
[/list]

[b]1.1.0[/b]
[list]
[*]The mod's text in all 15 languages the game supports, following the game's language (or [i]Language=[/i] in [i]minimap_config.ini[/i]). The map key widens to fit longer labels. Requested by Loling91.
[*]Find ignores upper and lower case in every script, finds places by their English type name in any language, and no longer cuts names in the middle of a character.
[*]Reported bugs fixed: none.
[/list]

[b]1.0.0[/b]
[list]
[*]First release.
[/list]

